course: dictionary
lesson: 4580
title: Words for helpers
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A helper is a person who helps someone do a job. In school, a helper can be a teaching assistant, a parent who helps on a trip, or a child given a job, like a «milk helper». Helper is a noun, so it names a person, and helpers is the plural for more than one.
explain: Look for clue words around a hard word. In «a mediator (a trained helper who helps them agree)», the words in brackets explain what helper means here. Brackets often give you the meaning straight away.
explain: In safety lessons you may hear «look for the helpers». Police officers, teachers and shop staff are helpers you can go to if you are lost or scared. In «ask a police officer or a steward (a helper in a bright vest at the event)», a steward is a kind of helper who works at an event.
fact: A helper is a person who helps someone do a job.
fact: «A classroom helper» is someone who helps out in the classroom.
fact: A mediator is a trained helper who helps people agree with each other.
fact: A steward is a helper in a bright vest at an event.
fact: In stories, little helpers, like Santa's elves, do work for others.
exercise: What is a helper? | A person who is always in charge | *A person who helps someone do a job | A bell that rings at break | A tool for cutting paper
exercise: In «a mediator (a trained helper who helps them agree)», what does helper mean? | *A trained person who helps others | A teacher who gives out tests | A person who goes on holiday | A loud person who shouts
exercise: Which of these is a helper at school? | A goldfish in a tank | A printer ink cartridge | *A teaching assistant | A rainy day
test: If you are lost in a crowd, who could you ask for help? | A loud bell | A pencil case | *A police officer | A cloud
test: In a safety lesson, «look for the helpers» means | *There are people you can go to if you are lost or scared | Run home alone | Helpers only live in stories | Hide under a table
exam: In the story of Odysseus, who were his helpers when he drove the men out of his hall? | Toad and the Wind in the Willows | The men feasting in the hall | Penelope's suitors | *His son and loyal helpers
